  "id": "COMPOUND:25472 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 3Beta-Acetoxy-8Beta-Isobutyryloxyreynosin may be involved in the regulation of SK-VLB through multiple indirect pathways. The compound is implicated in targeting VMRC-LCP, which in turn is a target of Oxytroflavoside B, and also targets (7S,11S)-(+)-12-acetoxysydonic acid, which ultimately leads to SK-VLB. Additionally, the compound is linked to Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which targets a different compound that also leads to SK-VLB. These findings collectively indicate that the compound may exert its effects on SK-VLB through a network of targets, possibly through signaling pathways or metabolic processes. The evidence is consistent with the compound acting as a modulator of downstream targets that ultimately influence SK-VLB, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
